Executive summaries of three World Bank regional economic updates of April
2026, each under CC BY 3.0 IGO, as stated on the World Bank Open Knowledge
Repository page and in the report ("This work is available under the Creative
Commons Attribution 3.0 IGO license"). Original work by The World Bank. These
are excerpts: this is an adaptation of an original work by The World Bank.
Views and opinions expressed in the adaptation are the sole responsibility of
the author or authors of the adaptation and are not endorsed by The World
Bank. Third-party material that the reports credit to others is not covered
by this licence. The World Bank's name and logo are not licensed; the covers
(which carry the logo) are left out.

- "Africa Economic Update, April 2026 (executive summary).pdf": World Bank,
  "Africa Economic Update, April 2026: Making Industrial Policy Work in
  Africa". https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/44533 .
  doi:10.1596/978-1-4648-2333-6 . CC BY 3.0 IGO. Excerpt: the Executive
  Summary (pages 2 to 10 of the published executive-summary file; its cover
  is left out).
- "Latin America and the Caribbean Economic Update, April 2026 (executive
  summary).pdf": William Maloney, Guillermo Vuletin and Andres Zambrano,
  "Revisiting Industrial Policy: Strategic Options for Today", Latin America
  and the Caribbean Economic Update (April 2026), World Bank.
  https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/44606 .
  doi:10.1596/978-1-4648-2337-4 . CC BY 3.0 IGO. Excerpt: the Executive
  Summary (pages xi to xviii of the report).
- "South Asia Economic Update, April 2026 (executive summary).pdf": World
  Bank, "South Asia Economic Update, April 2026: Working with Industrial
  Policy". https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/44482 .
  doi:10.1596/978-1-4648-2326-8 . CC BY 3.0 IGO. Excerpt: the Executive
  Summary file as published by the World Bank.


=== Reports and analysis, Chinese (reports/zh-CN/) ===

The Government Work Reports (政府工作报告) of 2024, 2025 and 2026, delivered by
the Premier of the State Council to the National People's Congress. Full
reports. They are not under a copyright licence, because they are not
protected by copyright. Article 5 of the Copyright Law of the People's
Republic of China (2020 revision, in force 1 June 2021) says:

  第五条　本法不适用于：
  （一）法律、法规，国家机关的决议、决定、命令和其他具有立法、行政、
  司法性质的文件，及其官方正式译文；
  （二）单纯事实消息；
  （三）历法、通用数表、通用表格和公式。

  Source: https://zscqj.beijing.gov.cn/zscqj/zwgk/flfg18/436481084/index.html
  (the law as published by a government body; the amending decision of the
  Standing Committee of the National People's Congress, 2020-11-11, is at
  https://www.ncac.gov.cn/xxfb/ywxx/202011/t20201112_47358.html ).

The Work Report is a report to the Congress that the Congress approves by
resolution, and sets out the
administrative plan of the State Council. We rely on that Article. The Chinese
government's site statement (https://www.gov.cn/home/2014-02/23/content_5046258.htm)
asks that its content not be distorted or altered; the words here are
unchanged.

Retrieved on 2026-10-10 from the State Council's website (www.gov.cn):

- "2024年政府工作报告.pdf": 《政府工作报告》, delivered 2024-03-05 at the
  second session of the 14th National People's Congress, 国务院总理 李强.
  https://www.gov.cn/yaowen/liebiao/202403/content_6939153.htm
- "2025年政府工作报告.pdf": 《政府工作报告》, delivered 2025-03-05 at the
  third session of the 14th National People's Congress, 国务院总理 李强.
  https://www.gov.cn/yaowen/liebiao/202503/content_7013163.htm
- "2026年政府工作报告.pdf": 《政府工作报告》, delivered 2026-03-05 at the
  fourth session of the 14th National People's Congress, 国务院总理 李强.
  https://www.gov.cn/yaowen/liebiao/202603/content_7062625.htm

The gov.cn pages offer no PDF, so we made the PDFs from the official text on
those pages. The words are unchanged, word for word and paragraph for
paragraph. The layout is ours (type, spacing, page breaks). Left out are the
page's wire-service dateline (新华社北京…电) and the photograph caption, which
are not part of the report.


=== Contracts and legal work, English (contracts/en/) ===

Three agreements from the Contract Understanding Atticus Dataset (CUAD) v1,
by The Atticus Project, under CC BY 4.0, as stated on its Zenodo record
(https://zenodo.org/records/4595826 , doi:10.5281/zenodo.4595826). Citation:
Dan Hendrycks, Collin Burns, Anya Chen and Spencer Ball, "CUAD: An
Expert-Annotated NLP Dataset for Legal Contract Review", NeurIPS 2021
Datasets and Benchmarks. The agreements are public exhibits filed with the
US Securities and Exchange Commission (EDGAR). The files are the dataset's
PDFs, unchanged in content, renamed.

- "Web Site Hosting Agreement (i-on interactive and Centrack).pdf": CUAD file
  full_contract_pdf/Part_II/Hosting/CENTRACKINTERNATIONALINC_10_29_1999-EX-10.3-WEB SITE HOSTING AGREEMENT.PDF .
- "Distributor Agreement (Snotarator and SMSA Ballinger).pdf": CUAD file
  full_contract_pdf/Part_III/Distributor/BLACKBOXSTOCKSINC_08_05_2014-EX-10.1-DISTRIBUTOR AGREEMENT.PDF .
- "Exclusive Distributor Agreement (Erchonia and InnerScope).pdf": CUAD file
  full_contract_pdf/Part_I/Distributor/InnerscopeHearingTechnologiesInc_20181109_8-K_EX-10.6_11419704_EX-10.6_Distributor Agreement.pdf .


